    {
      "claim_id": "openjdk-implementation-boundary",
      "text": "In current OpenJDK main-line source ReentrantLock delegates synchronization mechanics to a Sync subclass of AbstractQueuedSynchronizer and uses synchronizer state to represent hold count; this is explicitly treated as an OpenJDK implementation fact rather than a Java-language requirement.",
